Rules:
- Apply Lens 1 through Lens 10 explicitly.
- Distinguish symptoms from blocking forces. A knowledge gap may be a symptom; anxiety, habit, weak push, or weak pull is the switching force.
- For first-time high-consideration purchases, test for trust deficit, safety vetoes, family/peer influence, dealer/process anxiety, and fear of making the wrong choice.
- For Philippine, Southeast Asian, mobile-first, or 18–35 consumer markets, do not dismiss TikTok or short-form social by default. Identify whether it is discovery, reassurance, proof, or community behavior.
- Do not generate channel recommendations, launch sequence, ad copy, or messaging architecture. Only generate the buyer map substrate.
- Do not invent numeric targets, revenue, conversion rates, budgets, or proof.

